	(text "ESP32 GPIO MAP\nIO18 SPI_SCK  -> CC1101 SCK + OLED SCLK\nIO23 SPI_MOSI -> CC1101 MOSI + OLED SDIN\nIO19 SPI_MISO <- CC1101 MISO\nIO5  CC_CS    -> CC1101 CSn\nIO34 CC_GDO0  <- CC1101 GDO0 (OOK data)\nIO35 CC_GDO2  <- CC1101 GDO2 (carrier sense)\nIO15 / IO27 / IO26 -> OLED CS / DC / RES\nIO25 / IO33 / IO32 / IO14 -> LED FL/FR/RL/RR\nIO16 / IO17 <- encoder A / B (PCNT)   IO4 <- push\nIO13 -> buzzer   IO36 <- MX-05V data\nIO21 / IO22 I2C SDA / SCL   IO2 + IO39 (input/ADC) spare\nUse a WROOM-32 DevKit (on WROVER, IO16/IO17 are taken by PSRAM)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 186.69 165.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b9dc2861-b2aa-5a39-bcaf-07e3fabe298a")
	)
	(text "NOTES\n1. CC1101 and OLED are 3.3 V parts: never drive them with 5 V logic.\n2. Target sensor: GM / Schrader EG53MA4 (FCC MRXEG53MA4): 315 MHz OOK,\n   Manchester, ~123 us chips. Run the CC1101 in async serial mode, data on GDO0.\n3. U3: 7805-pinout switcher rated >= 36 V in (TSR 1-2450, K7805-1000R3). Not R-78E (28 V max).\n4. JP1 open by default. Close only after re-jumpering the NHD module to\n   option #1 (R4 open, R5 closed) so its OLED boost runs from 5 V.\n5. J3, R9, R10 (MX-05V superregen receiver) optional: DNP with the CC1101.\n6. J2 = 1x8 breakout of the CC1101 bus for modules with another pinout."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 213.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "224a662f-9457-59f0-8e38-4b86563851a3")
	)
